@startuml sequence_confirm_reservation
title Sequence — Confirm reservation (UC8)

actor Admin
participant API
participant DB
participant NotificationService
actor Customer

Admin -> API: POST /reservations/{id}/confirm (JWT)

alt user is not an admin
  API --> Admin: 403 Forbidden
else admin
  API -> DB: Load reservation
  DB --> API: reservation / none

  alt reservation not found
    API --> Admin: 404 Not Found
  else reservation is not DRAFT
    API --> Admin: 409 Conflict (cannot be confirmed)
  else reservation is DRAFT
    API -> DB: Re-check availability (query CONFIRMED reservations)
    DB --> API: available / conflict

    alt available
      API -> DB: Update reservation state -> CONFIRMED (commit)
      API -> NotificationService: send_confirmation(reservation, user)
      NotificationService --> Customer: confirmation (log, or e-mail if SMTP is configured)
      NotificationService --> API: sent / failed
      API --> Admin: 200 OK (reservation CONFIRMED)
    else conflict
      API --> Admin: 409 Conflict (slot taken)
    end
  end
end

note over API,DB
  The re-check catches a slot that was confirmed earlier.
  Without transactional locking, two confirmations running
  at the same moment could still both pass (known risk).
end note

note over NotificationService
  A failed e-mail is only logged —
  the reservation stays CONFIRMED.
end note

@enduml
